{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-10-16","kind":"proposition","title":"性质与证明：不可公度量与可公度量","englishTitle":"If two incommensurable magnitudes be added together, the whole will also be incommensurable with each of them; and, if the whole be incommensurable with one of them, the original magnitudes will also be incommensurable.","book":10,"number":16,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.16","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.16/","group":"prop_1","sourceNumber":16,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","contentId":"euclid-10-16","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"045981804b9089683c60409b6b3c6f65916bb986dea5569d48a4daba909567cd","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-10-16.statement","euclid-10-16.construction.1","euclid-10-16.proof.1","euclid-10-16.construction.2","euclid-10-16.proof.2","euclid-10-16.proof.3","euclid-10-16.proof.4","euclid-10-16.proof.5","euclid-10-16.proof.6","euclid-10-16.proof.7","euclid-10-16.proof.8","euclid-10-16.proof.9","euclid-10-16.proof.10","euclid-10-16.construction.3","euclid-10-16.proof.11","euclid-10-16.proof.12","euclid-10-16.proof.13","euclid-10-16.proof.14","euclid-10-16.proof.15","euclid-10-16.proof.16","euclid-10-16.construction.4","euclid-10-16.proof.17","euclid-10-16.conclusion","euclid-10-16.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-10-16.statement","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"2310b9c44c786623453b5c2f8248e78f13b4d335d98d0fa09157d53bd24e3102","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If two incommensurable magnitudes be added together, the whole will also be incommensurable with each of them; and, if the whole be incommensurable with one of them, the original magnitudes will also be incommensurable."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果将两个不可公度级加在一起,则每个不可公度级加在一起;如果一个不可公度级加在一起,则原来的不可公度级加在一起。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"4cd771702eb49cee0112724f30c949ca8b41a17710b789d9c6b48f3c9ed4f7b9","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let the two incommensurable magnitudes AB, BC be added together; I say that the whole AC is also incommensurable with each of the magnitudes AB, BC."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"将两个不可公度级的AB,BC加在一起;我说,整个AC级的每个级的AB,BC。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"5ee21c9c4cab7c64d70c983d3a87bd8a50b4bd67dffce48bd111d992017df7c9","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, if CA, AB are not incommensurable, some magnitude will measure them."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果CA,AB不是不可公度, 一定能测量它们。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.construction.2","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":3,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"17f0466b09e207c9d37101336cb7aa959f33a356cbecda1e4fb8fab0beb20cff","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let it measure them, if possible, and let it be D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果可能的话,让它衡量,然后让它达到D。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"66d7e137d391a0c2e6371aac8af7384165d1b1defaf6cc8bd28ea4a9895a6102","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Since then D measures CA, AB, therefore it will also measure the remainder BC."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,从那时起,D 整除 CA AB 名法官将同时完成其余的BC名法官的职务。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"496700060f1665c9c8f1325419f2d51cbb5b89897655dec6bed85956c4fa3e94","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But it measures AB also; therefore D measures AB, BC."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但该措施也针对AB措施,因此,D措施针对AB措施,BC措施针对AB措施。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":6,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"2aeb5b167d34c49939cfa15f41e56283ceedb9494a6077f20eb389d5d225b36a","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore AB, BC are commensurable; but they were also, by hypothesis, incommensurable: which is impossible."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,AB,BC是可公度;但根据假设,它们也是不可公度:这是不可能的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.proof.5","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":7,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"f99e1ea3149de122096c091a287ca5b03657b2868051903c305a9ad7c3223e64","citations":["euclid-10-def-1"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore no magnitude will measure CA, AB; therefore CA, AB are incommensurable. [[X. Def. 1](/principles/euclid-10-def-1)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,任何数值都无法测量CA,AB;因此,CA,AB是不可公度。 [[X. Def. 1](/principles/euclid-10-def-1)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.proof.6","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":8,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 6","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"7c9f1449fc7e78cffca36673a8b9ce8f11714c166090e0e92fd05874ecb67bdf","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Similarly we can prove that AC, CB are also incommensurable."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"同样,我们可以证明AC,CB也是不可公度。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.proof.7","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":9,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 7","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"0afc32097ffbbc18a5d92ea0902c8c92dfe2b731d18644402924265166317549","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore AC is incommensurable with each of the magnitudes AB, BC."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,AC是不可公度,每个星号AB,BC。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.proof.8","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":10,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 8","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"989ed63672d9168d57397e664334247861a2e46acc1d428a19cc96c8ab0b56ac","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Next, let AC be incommensurable with one of the magnitudes AB, BC."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"接下来,AC是不可公度, 大小之一AB,BC。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.proof.9","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":11,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 9","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"8f2c586f506a2256b41301d757875fa5379964ea7541ba61f3048863f361f36d","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"First, let it be incommensurable with AB; I say that AB, BC are also incommensurable."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"首先,让我们来讨论不可公度和AB;我说AB和BC也是不可公度。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.proof.10","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":12,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 10","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"8a8bf44468cbd411d245e0a388bb31c9f690039cccf7dd0145be4d971a9f2a80","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, if they are commensurable, some magnitude will measure them."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因为,如果它们是可公度, 一定能测量它们。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.construction.3","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":13,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"e4023240b77729bcadebbe7b10254e433a09394011854e25aa091ba7eba06863","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let it measure them, and let it be D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让它测量它们,让它达到D。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.proof.11","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":14,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 11","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"7b25f660c637f0a5ec3e3e4ce5c757f65a24ff808b0e281564e9e5b6c4e2fb3f","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Since then D measures AB, BC. therefore it will also measure the whole AC."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,从那时起,它还将对D项措施进行衡量。（相关点与线段：AB、BC、AC）"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.proof.12","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":15,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 12","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"57e94b42b375ed008cb8b8d7c0219536c513253698ecece09c743e3cafce32a7","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But it measures AB also; therefore D measures CA, AB."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但该措施也针对AB措施,因此,D措施针对CA措施,AB措施针对AB措施。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.proof.13","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":16,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 13","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c775b0daaa27aa6561320e9972ea74bbe22db5aab1a1dd312771c780e3cbcf83","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore CA, AB are commensurable; but they were also, by hypothesis, incommensurable: which is impossible."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,CA,AB是可公度;但根据假设,它们也是不可公度:这是不可能的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.proof.14","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":17,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 14","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"92327e1c3d229299b38c94fb206f173956653d92094b9e5abbbba2401c50c94b","citations":["euclid-10-def-1"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore no magnitude will measure AB, BC; therefore AB, BC are incommensurable. [[X. Def. 1](/principles/euclid-10-def-1)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,任何数值都无法测量AB,BC;因此,AB,BC是不可公度。 [[X. Def. 1](/principles/euclid-10-def-1)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.proof.15","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":18,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 15","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"6d0def46992eb0b105b82d6bce6477450c524a884c436026a0e1ed896becf6c9","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore etc."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"由此命题得证。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.proof.16","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":19,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 16","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"ae105839cc1b2df510411090e98600e2bbce44cd522ca9a2eebe60e94bbbf90c","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Lemma. If to any straight line there be applied a parallelogram deficient by a square figure, the applied parallelogram is equal to the rectangle contained by the segments of the straight line resulting from the application."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"引理. 如果对任何直线应用平行四边形的误差正方形, 应用的平行四边形等于由应用产生的直线各部分组成的矩形。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.construction.4","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":20,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"ae6de6e1c19a7fc65d2595e6ab1335795332f73835f5075bf28e09bbe516e698","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let there be applied to the straight line AB the parallelogram AD deficient by the square figure DB; I say that AD is equal to the rectangle contained by AC, CB."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"将平行四边形 AD线的正方形图DB的缺陷适用于直线 AB;我说,AD等于AC、CB组成的矩形。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.proof.17","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":21,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 17","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"05d217b8bf486df6b204ff9f9aed6904b1ade90b87041a3d4e754eb04cce0f5f","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"This is indeed at once manifest; for, since DB is a square, DC is equal to CB; and AD is the rectangle AC, CD, that is, the rectangle AC, CB."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"这确实是一次显示;因为DB是正方形,DC等于CB;AD是矩形,AC,CD,即矩形,AC,CB。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":22,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"6d0def46992eb0b105b82d6bce6477450c524a884c436026a0e1ed896becf6c9","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore etc."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"由此命题得证。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-16.source","contentId":"euclid-10-16","revisionId":"euclid-10-16@raw-045981804b908968","order":23,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"1b7cd88a